  "issue": {
    "body": "Hi,dear  commiter:\r\n     When I use the class  -- <JsonResponse>  to serialize(jsonify) a response, I find that I can not assign the special JsonEncoder .  Sometime i have to rewrite the JsonResponse class  ,like  following code\r\n`class JSONResponse(Response):\r\n    media_type = \"application/json\"\r\n\r\n    def __init__(self,*args,**kwargs):\r\n        self.encoder = kwargs.get('encoder',None)\r\n        super().__init__(*args)\r\n\r\n    def render(self, content: typing.Any) -> bytes:\r\n        return json.dumps(\r\n            content,\r\n            ensure_ascii=False,\r\n            allow_nan=False,\r\n            indent=None,\r\n            separators=(\",\", \":\"),\r\n            cls=self.encoder,\r\n        ).encode(\"utf-8\")`\r\n\r\n i think it's  necessary that provide custom jsonencoder function.  ",
    "closed_at": "2021-12-14T18:55:50Z",
    "created_at": "2021-07-22T09:24:00Z",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/Kludex/starlette/issues/1250",
    "number": 1250,
    "state": "closed",
    "title": "Could  JSONResponse  provide  JsonEncoder class option on    JSONResponse.__init__ () ?",
    "user": "lishukan"
  },
